1
00:00:42,967 --> 00:00:47,257
<i>Memories that persist through 30 million years...</i>

2
00:00:48,297 --> 00:00:51,487
<i>In the never-stopping, never-reversing,</i>

3
00:00:52,427 --> 00:00:54,707
<i>never-changing flux,</i>

4
00:00:56,437 --> 00:00:59,707
<i>feelings are memories that cross time.</i>

5
00:01:00,857 --> 00:01:04,967
<i>Feelings are memories that have reached the gate of fate.</i>

6
00:01:12,447 --> 00:01:13,807
A dream?

7
00:01:42,337 --> 00:01:47,127
Karamatta ito ga kishimi atte

8
00:01:42,337 --> 00:01:47,127
The intertwined threads compete

9
00:01:47,127 --> 00:01:53,567
mujun teiku wo uwagaki suru

10
00:01:47,127 --> 00:01:53,567
Overwriting any contradictory takes

11
00:01:53,677 --> 00:01:58,507
Rifujin wa itsuka konsen shite

12
00:01:53,677 --> 00:01:58,507
Irrationality is going haywire

13
00:01:58,507 --> 00:02:04,487
ai mo mirai sae mo koroshite yuku

14
00:01:58,507 --> 00:02:04,487
Putting our love and our future to death

15
00:02:05,027 --> 00:02:11,167
Bamen goto ni ukande kuru

16
00:02:05,027 --> 00:02:11,167
The scenes we shared come to mind

17
00:02:11,167 --> 00:02:16,397
kizuna mitaina sono zenbu ga

18
00:02:11,167 --> 00:02:16,397
All of them like bonds between us

19
00:02:16,397 --> 00:02:22,137
Mabushii hodo kagayai teru

20
00:02:16,397 --> 00:02:22,137
They shine in a blinding light

21
00:02:22,137 --> 00:02:27,957
bajji ni shirushita kakegae nai mono

22
00:02:22,137 --> 00:02:27,957
Inscribed on the irreplaceable badge

23
00:02:28,857 --> 00:02:30,277
I believe it

24
00:02:30,277 --> 00:02:35,907
Fly away sekai wa owari ga hajimaru

25
00:02:30,277 --> 00:02:35,907
Fly away as the world begins to end

26
00:02:35,907 --> 00:02:41,487
Futsugouna asu wo nomikonde ku

27
00:02:35,907 --> 00:02:41,487
The unwanted tomorrow will be consumed

28
00:02:41,487 --> 00:02:47,197
Loneliness kodoku no deja vu ni toraware

29
00:02:41,487 --> 00:02:47,197
Loneliness, imprisoned in the déjà vu of solitude

30
00:02:47,197 --> 00:02:52,817
Kaisen wa yagate tachikira reta

31
00:02:47,197 --> 00:02:52,817
The circuit is finally severed

32
00:02:52,817 --> 00:02:58,497
Ichiga kiete zeroni naru ishiki no surikae

33
00:02:52,817 --> 00:02:58,497
"1" disappears and becomes "0" as a consciousness is usurped

34
00:02:58,497 --> 00:03:04,737
Anata no me wa ima nani wo utsushi teru no?

35
00:02:58,497 --> 00:03:04,737
What do those eyes of yours reflect now?

36
00:03:15,017 --> 00:03:16,847
Hey, you there.

37
00:03:17,097 --> 00:03:20,997
Can you see us? Why don't you answer us?

38
00:03:20,997 --> 00:03:24,227
I'm talking to you, with the dumb expression!

39
00:03:23,137 --> 00:03:24,897
Tutturu~

40
00:03:24,897 --> 00:03:26,397
I'm Mayushii!

41
00:03:26,397 --> 00:03:29,237
Hey, Lab Member No. 003, Supah Hakah.

42
00:03:29,507 --> 00:03:31,267
Say something.

43
00:03:31,267 --> 00:03:34,117
It's "Hacker," not "Hakah," duh!

44
00:03:34,397 --> 00:03:37,027
He never says anything.

45
00:03:37,027 --> 00:03:39,267
But there has been a development.

46
00:03:39,267 --> 00:03:42,167
Thanks to a year of persistent effort,

47
00:03:42,437 --> 00:03:45,627
due to our inquisitive minds, he produced offspring!

48
00:03:46,377 --> 00:03:48,117
So cute!

49
00:03:48,117 --> 00:03:49,757
Normalfags should just get out.

50
00:03:49,757 --> 00:03:53,507
It's only logical to assume that somewhere within this software lies

51
00:03:53,507 --> 00:03:57,507
the secret code to reconstructing this world's ruling structure!

52
00:03:57,507 --> 00:04:02,387
I'll uncover it at any cost! On my name, Hououin Kyouma!

53
00:04:03,447 --> 00:04:05,777
Daru, do you want some barley tea?

54
00:04:05,777 --> 00:04:07,357
Yes, please.

55
00:04:07,617 --> 00:04:12,127
Mayushii, when you serve tea you should say, "Here's your tea."

56
00:04:12,127 --> 00:04:13,647
"Here's your tea?"

57
00:04:13,647 --> 00:04:16,897
Yeah. "I'll leave your tea here," is good too.

58
00:04:16,897 --> 00:04:18,457
And you, Okarin?

59
00:04:18,457 --> 00:04:23,207
Do you think I could drink the beverage of commoners?

60
00:04:23,207 --> 00:04:26,487
I only consume the intellectual drink of the chosen ones!

61
00:04:26,487 --> 00:04:27,537
Dr Pepper, right?

62
00:04:29,497 --> 00:04:30,207
Mayuri.

63
00:04:30,517 --> 00:04:34,087
Switch on Future Gadget No.10 Cool Visitor!

64
00:04:34,087 --> 00:04:38,927
But it doesn't cool the air very well...

65
00:04:38,927 --> 00:04:41,267
Don't you worry.

66
00:04:41,267 --> 00:04:44,577
It's been half a day since we suspended continuous operation.

67
00:04:44,577 --> 00:04:47,567
It's got plenty of cool air inside.

68
00:04:47,567 --> 00:04:49,317
Really?

69
00:04:51,317 --> 00:04:53,487
So? Feels good, right?

70
00:04:53,487 --> 00:04:56,057
It doesn't feel any different from a normal fan.

71
00:04:56,057 --> 00:04:59,987
Actually, the heat released by the motor is stronger than the cold air.

72
00:05:00,747 --> 00:05:03,917
The tea doesn't feel that cold anymore, either...

73
00:05:03,917 --> 00:05:07,617
Be silent! A new discovery is just around the corner and—

74
00:05:10,547 --> 00:05:15,797
Just shutting off like that is the worst possible thing that could happen to my data!

75
00:05:17,547 --> 00:05:19,177
You—!

76
00:05:20,217 --> 00:05:25,307
If I lose all of my game character data, I'll kill you, and then commit suicide!

77
00:05:24,247 --> 00:05:25,307
Tears?

78
00:05:25,307 --> 00:05:26,767
Okabe!

79
00:05:26,767 --> 00:05:27,367
Oh, no!

80
00:05:27,367 --> 00:05:29,187
You bastard! Get down here!

81
00:05:29,617 --> 00:05:33,987
If you need something, then <i>you</i> should come upstairs, Mr. Braun!

82
00:05:33,987 --> 00:05:36,737
Shut it! I'll add 5,000 yen to your rent!

83
00:05:36,737 --> 00:05:37,817
I'll be right there!

84
00:05:38,567 --> 00:05:40,147
Nae!

85
00:05:40,147 --> 00:05:43,197
Mayuri!

86
00:05:43,197 --> 00:05:47,867
Braun Tube Studio

87
00:05:43,197 --> 00:05:49,457
Future Gadget Lab

88
00:05:44,027 --> 00:05:46,307
<i>Summer 2010.</i>

89
00:05:46,907 --> 00:05:49,457
<i>One year has passed since I reached</i>

90
00:05:49,847 --> 00:05:51,387
<i>the Steins Gate world line.</i>

91
00:05:52,357 --> 00:05:56,297
<i>Mayuri is alive. Kurisu wasn't killed</i>

92
00:05:57,297 --> 00:06:01,217
<i>and neither the time machine nor D-mail exist in this world.</i>

93
00:06:01,897 --> 00:06:07,077
<i>Time proceeds only forward, never backward,</i>

94
00:06:07,077 --> 00:06:09,377
<i>the future doesn't change,</i>

95
00:06:09,377 --> 00:06:13,397
<i>and there isn't a single other world line in existence...</i>

96
00:06:13,397 --> 00:06:14,027
Mayuri—

97
00:06:37,277 --> 00:06:39,057
Okarin?

98
00:06:40,807 --> 00:06:42,487
What's wrong?

99
00:06:42,487 --> 00:06:44,097
Nothing...

100
00:06:44,487 --> 00:06:45,967
Listen, Okarin.

101
00:06:47,017 --> 00:06:49,067
Are you sure?

102
00:06:49,067 --> 00:06:53,687
Yes, the survival of my Future Gadget Lab depends on

103
00:06:53,687 --> 00:06:55,727
this mission I have to clear.

104
00:06:56,077 --> 00:06:58,217
The important mission Mr. Braun entrusted to me is—

105
00:06:58,217 --> 00:07:02,637
Oh. Well, Ruka is waiting for me, so see you later.

106
00:07:10,217 --> 00:07:13,477
Welcome back. Are you here on your summer holiday?

107
00:07:13,477 --> 00:07:15,627
Not your business.

108
00:07:16,297 --> 00:07:19,007
Isn't she here yet?

109
00:07:19,007 --> 00:07:23,217
It landed a while ago. She shouldn't be long...

110
00:07:27,877 --> 00:07:29,637
Kurisu!

111
00:07:29,997 --> 00:07:32,267
Welcome back!

112
00:07:32,857 --> 00:07:36,267
Mayuri! You came all the way here to pick me up?

113
00:07:36,267 --> 00:07:40,267
Yep. I couldn't wait!

114
00:07:40,887 --> 00:07:42,857
Long time no see.

115
00:07:42,857 --> 00:07:46,867
Indeed... Urushibara, right?

116
00:07:46,867 --> 00:07:48,577
Yes.

117
00:07:48,577 --> 00:07:50,077
<i>But he's a guy.</i>

118
00:07:51,247 --> 00:07:53,247
You'll stop by the lab, right?

119
00:07:54,077 --> 00:07:57,587
Y-Yes... it's still early, so...

120
00:07:58,527 --> 00:08:01,567
The station has changed a lot too.

121
00:08:01,567 --> 00:08:06,297
Yep, there's a new GunBam Cafe, and an idol bar...

122
00:08:06,297 --> 00:08:08,887
Even Radio Kaikan's been rebuilt.

123
00:08:09,367 --> 00:08:12,597
A lot's changed in a year, I guess. What about the lab?

124
00:08:13,597 --> 00:08:16,517
No particular change there, I guess...

125
00:08:16,517 --> 00:08:20,477
Oh, but... Daru made a friend!

126
00:08:21,017 --> 00:08:22,187
A girl!

127
00:08:22,517 --> 00:08:23,357
You're kidding!

128
00:08:23,357 --> 00:08:29,087
She's a cosplayer, Amane...Yuki?

129
00:08:29,087 --> 00:08:32,897
Yes. I heard they met online.

130
00:08:32,897 --> 00:08:34,987
She's very pretty.

131
00:08:34,987 --> 00:08:36,787
Pret... ty?

132
00:08:37,077 --> 00:08:38,527
Here she is.

133
00:08:38,527 --> 00:08:41,057
Is... Hashida's family rich or something?

134
00:08:41,057 --> 00:08:43,137
Don't think so...

135
00:08:43,137 --> 00:08:45,507
Then he must have won the lottery.

136
00:08:45,507 --> 00:08:48,047
I didn't hear about anything like that either...

137
00:08:48,047 --> 00:08:49,367
Then...

138
00:08:49,367 --> 00:08:51,527
It's Daru!

139
00:08:51,527 --> 00:08:53,187
Daru!

140
00:08:53,187 --> 00:08:55,937
Mayu—! It's Miss Makise?! Long time—

141
00:08:55,937 --> 00:08:58,027
If you're trying to trick her, come clean!

142
00:08:58,027 --> 00:09:00,897
What are you talking about?

143
00:09:03,607 --> 00:09:06,347
Trick? Daru?

144
00:09:06,347 --> 00:09:08,777
I don't think that's the case...

145
00:09:09,047 --> 00:09:12,527
You said you exchanged photos the other day, right?

146
00:09:12,527 --> 00:09:14,607
What kind of photo did you send?

147
00:09:14,607 --> 00:09:16,167
Well...

148
00:09:17,977 --> 00:09:19,417
Photoshop, huh.

149
00:09:19,817 --> 00:09:24,767
Of course. No girl would go near such a pervert otherwise.

150
00:09:24,767 --> 00:09:27,257
That's mean! Don't judge!

151
00:09:27,257 --> 00:09:31,937
But she said her type is bear-like guys, didn't she?

152
00:09:31,937 --> 00:09:33,237
Y-Yeah...

153
00:09:33,237 --> 00:09:35,557
Don't you dare assume that a woman saying

154
00:09:35,557 --> 00:09:38,197
"Bear-like guys are my type" means "I'm into fat guys!"

155
00:09:38,197 --> 00:09:39,767
What's that? You're scary!

156
00:09:46,407 --> 00:09:48,937
Messy as always.

157
00:09:48,937 --> 00:09:50,407
Kurisu.

158
00:09:50,407 --> 00:09:51,867
Here's your tea.

159
00:09:51,867 --> 00:09:53,567
Thx!

160
00:09:54,717 --> 00:09:57,457
You still talk like an @channel user...

161
00:09:57,457 --> 00:09:58,367
Shut up!

162
00:09:59,057 --> 00:10:01,657
But Okarin sure is late.

163
00:10:01,657 --> 00:10:03,127
He said that after the errand for Mr. Braun,

164
00:10:03,587 --> 00:10:06,627
he'd go to Ameyoko to buy something.

165
00:10:06,627 --> 00:10:08,887
But Miss Makise took the trouble to come over...

166
00:10:08,887 --> 00:10:10,627
It-It's no big deal!

167
00:10:17,187 --> 00:10:19,497
Kurisu, are you all right?

168
00:10:19,497 --> 00:10:21,477
I'm very all right, Mayuri.

169
00:10:21,797 --> 00:10:24,897
Actually, I'm almost relieved he's not here!

170
00:10:24,897 --> 00:10:27,607
Don't need to waste any energy...

171
00:10:27,607 --> 00:10:29,817
Template: Tsundere Queen.

172
00:10:29,817 --> 00:10:31,907
I'm neither tsun nor dere!

173
00:10:31,907 --> 00:10:34,327
Darn that Mr. Braun!

174
00:10:34,327 --> 00:10:37,197
He chose a faraway store on purpose!

175
00:10:46,207 --> 00:10:48,217
It's me. Yes...

176
00:10:48,487 --> 00:10:51,657
Looks like a new agent from the Organization.

177
00:10:51,657 --> 00:10:54,277
What?! An emergency request?

178
00:10:54,837 --> 00:10:58,957
I got it. If that's Steins;Gate's choice...

179
00:10:59,707 --> 00:11:02,187
"El Psy Kongroo."

180
00:11:02,187 --> 00:11:04,317
Still as annoying as usual.

181
00:11:04,627 --> 00:11:05,687
Sorry.

182
00:11:05,687 --> 00:11:07,847
Long time no see, assistant.

183
00:11:07,847 --> 00:11:13,087
I mean, Cristina.
 No, experiment-loving perverted girl.

184
00:11:13,087 --> 00:11:14,987
"Pervert" for short!

185
00:11:14,987 --> 00:11:17,907
There's a limit to rudeness!

186
00:11:17,907 --> 00:11:22,847
Hah! That reaction... It seems you are the real Cristina.

187
00:11:22,847 --> 00:11:24,327
Cristina!

188
00:11:24,327 --> 00:11:26,707
There's no "tina"!

189
00:11:26,707 --> 00:11:28,207
But, Cristina!

190
00:11:28,537 --> 00:11:32,537
The Future Gadget Lab is a secret state organization.

191
00:11:32,537 --> 00:11:36,797
It's only natural that to get in, you need proper authorization.

192
00:11:36,797 --> 00:11:38,057
Remember that.

193
00:11:38,057 --> 00:11:42,017
I'm a lab member. I have the right to come and go as I please!

194
00:11:42,017 --> 00:11:46,597
You haven't shown up for a year
 and dare make such a wild claim?

195
00:11:46,597 --> 00:11:51,427
And you call yourself my assistant?!

196
00:11:47,897 --> 00:11:51,427
It feels like being back in the old lab.

197
00:11:51,427 --> 00:11:54,907
I said I'm not your assistant nor am I Cristina!

198
00:11:51,437 --> 00:11:54,907
Yes, Mayushii is very happy.

199
00:11:54,907 --> 00:11:58,367
By the way, experiment-loving perverted genius girl?

200
00:11:58,807 --> 00:11:59,457
No!

201
00:11:59,457 --> 00:12:02,357
Why did you come to Japan, pervert girl?

202
00:12:02,357 --> 00:12:04,597
To apologize for not showing up at the lab?

203
00:12:04,597 --> 00:12:07,417
Why should I apologize?!

204
00:12:07,417 --> 00:12:10,337
There's a conference here in Japan, so I just dropped by!

205
00:12:10,617 --> 00:12:12,337
And I wanted to see Mayuri too.

206
00:12:13,387 --> 00:12:15,137
Here's a souvenir.

207
00:12:15,137 --> 00:12:18,217
Really?! Thank you!

208
00:12:19,007 --> 00:12:21,807
It's a sewing set I found in the US.

209
00:12:21,807 --> 00:12:23,897
This is for you, Urushibara.

210
00:12:23,897 --> 00:12:25,267
Thank you so much!

211
00:12:25,267 --> 00:12:29,027
And for me, some uncensored American version of something...

212
00:12:29,027 --> 00:12:31,107
Customs would arrest me!

213
00:12:31,477 --> 00:12:36,407
There's nothing for you guys! I only came to see Mayuri and Urushibara.

214
00:12:39,327 --> 00:12:42,677
I wasn't expecting anything in the least!

215
00:12:42,677 --> 00:12:47,087
Now that you understand, leave this place at once!

216
00:12:47,087 --> 00:12:49,767
You don't need to tell me! I was going anyway!

217
00:12:49,767 --> 00:12:51,837
I need to check into the hotel.

218
00:12:51,837 --> 00:12:54,417
What? You're leaving already?

219
00:12:54,417 --> 00:12:58,197
I'll be in Japan for a while. I'll get in touch with you again.

220
00:12:59,677 --> 00:13:02,757
Sorry for the wait, Kyouma! Nyan~!

221
00:13:03,357 --> 00:13:05,227
Sorry for intruding...

222
00:13:05,227 --> 00:13:08,597
Faris and Moeka! What are you two doing here?

223
00:13:08,597 --> 00:13:11,067
What? Aren't we having a barbecue? Nyan~!

224
00:13:11,627 --> 00:13:13,937
Kyouma just came by and said, nyan~,

225
00:13:13,937 --> 00:13:18,767
that we should have a barbecue today because Ku-nyan is coming.

226
00:13:19,447 --> 00:13:21,367
I... got a mail...

227
00:13:21,367 --> 00:13:22,197
Okarin...

228
00:13:22,197 --> 00:13:25,377
What's this? Due to the increasing activity of a solar storm,

229
00:13:25,377 --> 00:13:28,827
auditory hallucinations and unlikely telecommunications are occurring?!

230
00:13:29,527 --> 00:13:33,587
Don't tell me the Seven Sages of Seiryuzan have sprung into actionyan!?

231
00:13:33,587 --> 00:13:37,107
That's unforgivable! I'll demand an apology!

232
00:13:37,107 --> 00:13:37,887
Calm down, please!

233
00:13:37,887 --> 00:13:41,147
The fact that all the lab members have been reunited here

234
00:13:41,147 --> 00:13:42,847
is Steins;Gate's choice.

235
00:13:43,307 --> 00:13:45,807
Mayuri! Prepare for the round table meeting!

236
00:13:45,807 --> 00:13:46,797
Okay!

237
00:13:46,797 --> 00:13:47,937
Rukako!

238
00:13:47,937 --> 00:13:49,267
Y-Yes!

239
00:13:49,267 --> 00:13:51,517
You didn't say the password.

240
00:13:51,907 --> 00:13:56,357
E... El Psy... Kongree?

241
00:13:56,357 --> 00:13:58,527
It's "Kongroo," Ruka.

242
00:13:58,527 --> 00:14:00,527
Kurisu, you do have time, right?

243
00:14:00,527 --> 00:14:02,097
Kind of...

244
00:14:02,097 --> 00:14:04,227
No more tsundere!

245
00:14:04,227 --> 00:14:05,537
You too, Okarin.

246
00:14:05,907 --> 00:14:09,507
<i>He can never be honest about his feelings...</i>

247
00:14:16,537 --> 00:14:23,347
Mix! Mix! Mix! Mix! Mix! Mix!

248
00:14:17,587 --> 00:14:22,547
Wow! Eye-contact Mix Mix Yakisoba!

249
00:14:23,917 --> 00:14:26,947
Oh, that may be a bit undercooked.

250
00:14:26,947 --> 00:14:28,257
No problem.

251
00:14:32,727 --> 00:14:34,437
<i>It </i>was<i> undercooked...</i>

252
00:14:40,487 --> 00:14:42,237
<i>The second was fine.</i>

253
00:14:42,237 --> 00:14:47,087
Oh! Nae, you can eat peppers?! I'm impressed!

254
00:14:47,087 --> 00:14:51,057
Yeah, but my daddy can't.

255
00:14:49,987 --> 00:14:52,157
<i>It's been a year...</i>

256
00:14:59,457 --> 00:15:01,707
What... was that?

257
00:15:02,177 --> 00:15:03,617
Okabe!

258
00:15:04,507 --> 00:15:06,087
What's up, Cristi—

259
00:15:06,087 --> 00:15:09,107
I'm just not convinced!

260
00:15:09,107 --> 00:15:10,307
What are you talking about?

261
00:15:10,307 --> 00:15:13,397
The time machine! It's impossible!

262
00:15:13,907 --> 00:15:15,247
Theoretically—!

263
00:15:15,247 --> 00:15:15,767
You're too close!

264
00:15:16,067 --> 00:15:18,557
Oh! Don't tell me you're—

265
00:15:19,147 --> 00:15:22,127
There should only be alcohol-free beer...

266
00:15:27,307 --> 00:15:30,677
Now this is real beer!

267
00:15:31,577 --> 00:15:33,327
Hey, are you listening?

268
00:15:33,327 --> 00:15:34,597
W-What?

269
00:15:34,597 --> 00:15:35,997
I'm talking about before!

270
00:15:36,457 --> 00:15:39,047
What you told me when you came to the States!

271
00:15:39,047 --> 00:15:43,367
About another world line, and that something happened to another me...

272
00:15:43,367 --> 00:15:47,077
Then you took advantage of the fact that I didn't understand

273
00:15:47,077 --> 00:15:49,807
and in the confusion, even did that thing...

274
00:15:50,927 --> 00:15:52,597
That... thing?

275
00:15:54,147 --> 00:15:58,067
W-Wait! Are you bringing that up here and now?!

276
00:15:58,067 --> 00:16:02,027
What? So it's really that shameful for you?

277
00:16:02,027 --> 00:16:05,347
No... that's not...

278
00:16:03,877 --> 00:16:06,407
You know, that time... I was quite...

279
00:16:07,197 --> 00:16:08,697
That time...

280
00:16:08,697 --> 00:16:10,307
H-Hey!

281
00:16:10,307 --> 00:16:11,767
Is something wrong, nyan~?

282
00:16:11,767 --> 00:16:12,867
N-Nothing!

283
00:16:12,867 --> 00:16:16,967
Faris' Special End of the Century Yakisoba's almost ready, nyan~!

284
00:16:16,967 --> 00:16:21,427
This guy hasn't even sent me a single email since last summer!

285
00:16:21,427 --> 00:16:23,937
Even after he did "that thing!"

286
00:16:23,937 --> 00:16:25,177
Telling me "I love you."

287
00:16:25,177 --> 00:16:28,007
Then blaming it on another word line—

288
00:16:29,737 --> 00:16:32,497
Give it a break. Come here!

289
00:16:33,547 --> 00:16:35,897
Let go of me!

290
00:16:38,147 --> 00:16:39,817
That was dangerous—

291
00:16:41,007 --> 00:16:42,437
Okabe...

292
00:16:42,437 --> 00:16:44,107
W-What?

293
00:16:44,767 --> 00:16:45,987
Hold me!

294
00:16:50,117 --> 00:16:51,827
H-Hey...

295
00:16:56,487 --> 00:16:59,287
Shave. Shave.

296
00:16:57,667 --> 00:16:59,287
Hey, you! Wait!

297
00:17:00,937 --> 00:17:02,757
Prickly.

298
00:17:03,577 --> 00:17:04,947
What if someone comes?!

299
00:17:04,947 --> 00:17:05,637
You don't want that?

300
00:17:05,637 --> 00:17:06,007
What?

301
00:17:06,007 --> 00:17:07,777
You don't want to be seen?

302
00:17:07,777 --> 00:17:10,097
No, it's not that...

303
00:17:10,097 --> 00:17:11,717
Then it's fine, right?

304
00:17:11,717 --> 00:17:13,387
No... but...

305
00:17:13,387 --> 00:17:17,517
Yes or no?! Which is Steins;Gate's choice?!

306
00:17:17,517 --> 00:17:19,147
No... I-I mean...

307
00:17:19,147 --> 00:17:20,897
You! Be clear!

308
00:17:22,397 --> 00:17:23,737
W-Wait!

309
00:17:35,207 --> 00:17:36,707
Here, assistant.

310
00:17:37,027 --> 00:17:39,037
Cool your head a bit.

311
00:17:39,577 --> 00:17:40,747
Thanks.

312
00:17:41,417 --> 00:17:42,547
Good grief...

313
00:17:42,547 --> 00:17:44,737
Good grief what?

314
00:17:44,737 --> 00:17:46,537
Trying to pick a fight again?

315
00:17:48,557 --> 00:17:51,347
I wish I could tell you.

316
00:17:52,017 --> 00:17:55,727
I'm a scientist. I don't want to accept the idea of

317
00:17:55,727 --> 00:17:58,307
past life encounters, destiny,

318
00:17:58,967 --> 00:18:02,027
and world lines... or time machines.

319
00:18:02,027 --> 00:18:03,067
I know that...

320
00:18:03,067 --> 00:18:06,647
But... even though I try to deny them in theory,

321
00:18:06,647 --> 00:18:08,567
something keeps bothering me...

322
00:18:09,227 --> 00:18:11,777
My head gets all messed up...

323
00:18:13,697 --> 00:18:15,347
T-This is...

324
00:18:18,667 --> 00:18:21,077
A spoon... and fork...

325
00:18:21,077 --> 00:18:23,787
You wanted them, so...

326
00:18:25,547 --> 00:18:28,377
Yes, I did...

327
00:18:28,777 --> 00:18:32,207
But I never told you that...

328
00:18:32,207 --> 00:18:34,767
<i>I see... It wasn't on this world line...</i>

329
00:18:36,117 --> 00:18:40,347
It feels like someone's been peeping on my thoughts...

330
00:18:41,567 --> 00:18:43,607
Sorry, I'm going to rest a bit.

331
00:18:53,917 --> 00:18:57,067
Okarin, there's going to be no yakisoba left for you!

332
00:19:00,577 --> 00:19:02,337
Hey... Mayuri.

333
00:19:03,627 --> 00:19:05,497
I told you before, right?

334
00:19:06,167 --> 00:19:09,857
That I came here from a different world line?

335
00:19:09,857 --> 00:19:15,347
Yes, you were with another Mayushii and another Kurisu, right?

336
00:19:15,677 --> 00:19:18,207
What do you think about that story?

337
00:19:18,207 --> 00:19:19,467
Why?

338
00:19:19,467 --> 00:19:22,437
Well... Kurisu is...

339
00:19:23,857 --> 00:19:31,557
Mayushii doesn't think Okarin's lying, so it must be true.

340
00:19:31,557 --> 00:19:36,827
But that's because Mayushii can't understand difficult things...

341
00:19:37,267 --> 00:19:39,767
Kurisu is really smart,

342
00:19:39,767 --> 00:19:44,797
so maybe she's thinking really hard about what Okarin said.

343
00:19:45,527 --> 00:19:47,967
I'll be upstairs, okay?

344
00:19:50,217 --> 00:19:52,177
A time machine...

345
00:19:59,387 --> 00:20:00,597
What?!

346
00:20:00,977 --> 00:20:01,977
Mayuri!

347
00:20:11,287 --> 00:20:12,527
Okarin,

348
00:20:12,847 --> 00:20:16,277
do you know where we put the new dish cloth?

349
00:20:16,277 --> 00:20:21,367
It's not on the shelf, so... maybe it's under the stove?

350
00:20:21,367 --> 00:20:23,947
Here it is! Mr. New Dish Cloth!

351
00:20:23,947 --> 00:20:26,957
What's wrong, Okarin?

352
00:20:26,957 --> 00:20:27,837
This is...?

353
00:20:35,757 --> 00:20:39,237
It's fun to eat outside, even if it's on top of the lab!

354
00:20:39,237 --> 00:20:44,017
A barbecue with Faris! My heart's on fire!

355
00:20:43,107 --> 00:20:44,017
Mayuri!

356
00:20:44,017 --> 00:20:44,837
What?

357
00:20:44,837 --> 00:20:45,597
Come this way!

358
00:20:45,597 --> 00:20:46,477
Okarin?! What's wrong?!

359
00:20:46,477 --> 00:20:47,897
Wake up, Kurisu!

360
00:20:47,897 --> 00:20:48,417
Quick!

361
00:20:48,417 --> 00:20:50,177
What's up with you?!

362
00:20:50,177 --> 00:20:51,027
Hurry!

363
00:20:54,707 --> 00:20:57,237
Okabe? What...

364
00:20:57,237 --> 00:20:57,907
Be quiet!

365
00:21:00,987 --> 00:21:04,087
Hey, you guys forgot this on the roof—

366
00:21:04,087 --> 00:21:04,947
Don't move!

367
00:21:05,597 --> 00:21:08,497
What the hell?! Okabe...

368
00:21:08,497 --> 00:21:10,547
Kurisu! The time leap-machine, quick!

369
00:21:11,377 --> 00:21:12,757
We don't have time! Quick!

370
00:21:12,757 --> 00:21:16,257
Okabe, calm down! There's no such thing here!

371
00:21:16,257 --> 00:21:18,597
What are you saying?! It's just over there—

372
00:21:29,047 --> 00:21:32,427
This is the Steins Gate world line?

373
00:21:33,567 --> 00:21:34,947
Steins?

374
00:21:34,947 --> 00:21:38,597
Yes, the world line you told me

375
00:21:38,597 --> 00:21:40,937
you finally reached.

376
00:21:43,697 --> 00:21:46,357
Is that right? I'm sorry...

377
00:21:52,607 --> 00:21:54,777
What the hell was that?

378
00:22:01,047 --> 00:22:04,927
<i>What was that just now?</i>

379
00:22:05,437 --> 00:22:07,897
<i>A dream? A delusion?</i>

380
00:22:08,727 --> 00:22:12,647
<i>No, it was real without a doubt.</i>

381
00:22:12,927 --> 00:22:15,357
<i>I was in another world line.</i>

382
00:22:15,627 --> 00:22:19,487
<i>But I'm not using a D-mail or the time machine...</i>

383
00:22:20,727 --> 00:22:24,407
<i>No, be rational! That can't be possible!</i>

384
00:22:24,407 --> 00:22:26,977
<i>It's a delusion, a daydream.</i>

385
00:22:26,977 --> 00:22:31,837
<i>The memories of another world line are just making it feel like reality—</i>

386
00:22:32,987 --> 00:22:35,047
What a nice view!

387
00:22:35,537 --> 00:22:40,007
Human beings are creatures who need time to unwind once in a while.

388
00:22:40,327 --> 00:22:43,967
I have more fun working on the time leap machine...

389
00:22:45,217 --> 00:22:50,187
It's so hot! Why is this happening to me?

390
00:22:50,647 --> 00:22:56,027
You're too fat, Daru. You should exercise more.

391
00:22:57,127 --> 00:22:58,177
What is this place?

392
00:22:58,177 --> 00:22:59,737
You're so sloppy!

393
00:23:00,447 --> 00:23:02,687
You won't survive if you continue like that.

394
00:23:02,687 --> 00:23:03,407
Suzuha...

395
00:23:05,237 --> 00:23:10,247
I will never forgive you.
 You drove my daddy to his death.

396
00:23:10,527 --> 00:23:11,837
I will never forgive you.

397
00:23:14,167 --> 00:23:17,417
Stop!

398
00:23:23,447 --> 00:23:26,607
They're getting... longer?

399
00:23:26,607 --> 00:23:27,847
Okarin.

400
00:23:33,127 --> 00:23:34,017
Mayuri...

401
00:23:34,017 --> 00:23:35,477
Are you okay?

402
00:23:36,337 --> 00:23:38,867
Yes, no need to worry.

403
00:23:39,367 --> 00:23:43,407
I'm sorry about earlier. My right arm

404
00:23:43,407 --> 00:23:46,407
went berserk against my will!

405
00:23:47,117 --> 00:23:50,787
That's okay. I was just a little scared.

406
00:23:50,787 --> 00:23:53,627
Oh, you're sweating a lot!

407
00:23:55,637 --> 00:23:57,137
Sorry...

408
00:23:57,137 --> 00:24:02,307
No problem. This is all Mayushii can do.

409
00:24:04,557 --> 00:24:06,717
Lately, Mayushii's been having a recurring dream

410
00:24:07,927 --> 00:24:12,717
where Okarin comes and saves Mayushii over and over again...

411
00:24:13,707 --> 00:24:18,747
It's Mayushii's fault you always look so sad...

412
00:24:19,707 --> 00:24:21,147
Mayuri.

413
00:24:23,847 --> 00:24:25,167
It's just a dream.

414
00:24:26,427 --> 00:24:27,687
Okarin...

415
00:24:28,187 --> 00:24:30,097
It's nothing but a dream.

416
00:24:30,907 --> 00:24:32,117
You're right.

417
00:24:35,407 --> 00:24:36,457
Let's go home.

418
00:24:36,457 --> 00:24:37,637
Okay.

419
00:24:39,707 --> 00:24:42,417
You hugged me like this that time too.

420
00:24:43,677 --> 00:24:46,177
Thank you, Okarin.

421
00:25:06,187 --> 00:25:08,157
Excuse me!

422
00:25:08,157 --> 00:25:11,657
No Cell Phones

423
00:25:15,547 --> 00:25:17,527
Good morning, Faris.

424
00:25:17,527 --> 00:25:19,417
Good mornyan!

425
00:25:21,287 --> 00:25:22,297
How is it?

426
00:25:23,837 --> 00:25:25,867
Not good, Manager.

427
00:25:25,867 --> 00:25:27,197
Not good?

428
00:25:28,417 --> 00:25:33,787
With this month's energy bill alone, we're already 28,568 yen in the red.

429
00:25:36,337 --> 00:25:39,017
Should I raise the rent for real?

430
00:25:58,777 --> 00:26:00,707
I came all the way to Japan.

431
00:26:01,157 --> 00:26:04,047
I'd like to relax in a hot bath at least once.

432
00:26:11,737 --> 00:26:12,597
Who is it?

433
00:26:14,967 --> 00:26:16,557
The maid?

434
00:26:19,747 --> 00:26:21,937
Didn't I put up the "Do Not Disturb" sign?

435
00:26:31,197 --> 00:26:33,677
Oh? What's this?

436
00:26:33,677 --> 00:26:34,737
Makise Kurisu.

437
00:26:36,207 --> 00:26:38,977
I don't have time, so I'll tell you only this.

438
00:26:38,977 --> 00:26:40,037
Who are you?!

439
00:26:40,037 --> 00:26:43,587
Cell phone, microwave oven,

440
00:26:44,227 --> 00:26:45,297
SERN.

441
00:26:46,047 --> 00:26:47,257
Don't forget.

442
00:26:48,137 --> 00:26:50,947
Don't forget, and you'll find a way.

443
00:26:50,947 --> 00:26:52,957
As long as you continue to observe...

444
00:26:54,847 --> 00:26:56,347
you will not fail...

445
00:27:11,837 --> 00:27:13,237
Who are you?

446
00:27:19,767 --> 00:27:21,157
Cell phone,

447
00:27:21,957 --> 00:27:24,877
microwave oven, SERN?

448
00:27:34,447 --> 00:27:36,177
What on earth was that?

449
00:27:36,667 --> 00:27:39,667
It didn't look like they stole anything, but...

450
00:27:40,477 --> 00:27:44,147
I'll move to another room. That was creepy.

451
00:27:45,767 --> 00:27:49,387
What was creepy... Cristina?

452
00:27:50,397 --> 00:27:54,187
N-Nothing in particular!

453
00:27:54,187 --> 00:27:58,287
It's not like something scary happened to me at the hotel...

454
00:27:58,287 --> 00:28:01,717
Never mind that! Why are you here?!

455
00:28:01,717 --> 00:28:04,067
That's my line.

456
00:28:04,067 --> 00:28:09,167
While removing the medals I amassed during my research known as "dirt,"

457
00:28:09,167 --> 00:28:12,877
I was recalling my own accomplishments.

458
00:28:13,617 --> 00:28:15,407
I don't wish to be disturbed!

459
00:28:15,407 --> 00:28:19,107
Unfortunately, this is neither the lab nor your home!

460
00:28:19,107 --> 00:28:20,177
Let me through!

461
00:28:20,177 --> 00:28:23,537
It's not like I enjoy doing laundry with you.

462
00:28:23,537 --> 00:28:25,837
Hey! Don't open without asking.

463
00:28:25,837 --> 00:28:27,767
Take your stuff out when it's done!

464
00:28:28,857 --> 00:28:32,897
Look at how ragged this lab coat's gotten.

465
00:28:33,387 --> 00:28:35,867
Assistant, those are Daru's...

466
00:28:36,167 --> 00:28:37,287
underpants.

467
00:28:44,407 --> 00:28:46,707
Good thing I had some antiseptic on me!

468
00:28:47,087 --> 00:28:50,047
Daru would be saddened if he saw the way you reacted.

469
00:28:50,387 --> 00:28:54,507
It's because you always wear that worn-out coat that I got confused!

470
00:28:54,507 --> 00:28:58,417
A worn-out lab coat is part of the scientific aesthetic.

471
00:28:58,417 --> 00:29:00,677
There's a limit!

472
00:29:02,527 --> 00:29:04,597
Look, the sleeve's torn.

473
00:29:05,177 --> 00:29:07,557
Give it to me. I'll stitch it for you.

474
00:29:11,897 --> 00:29:13,777
W-What?!

475
00:29:13,777 --> 00:29:16,927
No... It's nothing...

476
00:29:16,927 --> 00:29:19,537
It's normal to carry a sewing kit, even for me!

477
00:29:19,537 --> 00:29:21,507
Y-Yeah, that's right.

478
00:29:22,347 --> 00:29:23,827
This...

479
00:29:24,247 --> 00:29:26,247
It's the kind of coat we use in America.

480
00:29:26,807 --> 00:29:28,807
You should keep a spare.

481
00:29:28,807 --> 00:29:32,377
It was made in the US. It should be perfect for your height.

482
00:29:32,677 --> 00:29:37,257
Really? You bought it just for me?

483
00:29:37,257 --> 00:29:40,317
No! It's just a coincidence!

484
00:29:40,317 --> 00:29:42,557
I had an extra one, that's all.

485
00:29:43,517 --> 00:29:48,127
And since you gave me that spoon and fork...

486
00:29:54,187 --> 00:29:56,527
I'm warning you, though.

487
00:29:56,527 --> 00:29:59,477
Don't complain about how I do it.

488
00:29:59,477 --> 00:30:01,777
And I don't have any white thread, so...

489
00:30:03,897 --> 00:30:04,867
Right...

490
00:30:06,417 --> 00:30:07,367
What?

491
00:30:08,567 --> 00:30:09,287
Nothing...

492
00:30:11,847 --> 00:30:14,297
Is it about something that happened in another world line again?

493
00:30:15,107 --> 00:30:19,547
Yes... And yet, not so.

494
00:30:20,077 --> 00:30:23,177
What was that self-contradicting statement?

495
00:30:23,807 --> 00:30:27,907
There's no doubt that thanks to my Reading Steiner ability,

496
00:30:27,907 --> 00:30:32,267
I could observe other world lines and still retain memories of them.

497
00:30:32,997 --> 00:30:38,357
And among those countless world lines that continued to converge and diverge,

498
00:30:38,357 --> 00:30:39,897
I drifted

499
00:30:39,897 --> 00:30:44,797
and miraculously reached the only one I really wanted to be on.

500
00:30:45,367 --> 00:30:49,537
On this world line, you are sitting here with me,

501
00:30:49,537 --> 00:30:51,377
and Mayuri is working part-time at MayQueen...

502
00:30:51,827 --> 00:30:55,587
That's enough for me. I can't ask for more.

503
00:30:56,217 --> 00:30:57,337
Okabe...

504
00:30:57,687 --> 00:31:00,717
I wanted the you of this world line

505
00:31:00,717 --> 00:31:06,157
to get to know more about me,
 so maybe I've said more than I should.

506
00:31:06,157 --> 00:31:07,227
I'm sorry.

507
00:31:07,837 --> 00:31:09,617
What?

508
00:31:09,617 --> 00:31:10,767
That's all I have to say.

509
00:31:11,147 --> 00:31:13,517
Your hand has stopped, assistant!

510
00:31:13,797 --> 00:31:16,657
I-I know! But...

511
00:31:17,377 --> 00:31:21,667
I just wonder if everything you said is true...

512
00:31:21,667 --> 00:31:23,787
It is only natural to doubt

513
00:31:24,317 --> 00:31:27,047
the existence of world lines...

514
00:31:27,047 --> 00:31:27,997
It's not that.

515
00:31:28,547 --> 00:31:32,107
If countless world lines do exist,

516
00:31:32,107 --> 00:31:37,087
I can hardly believe that only you retain memories of them.

517
00:31:37,467 --> 00:31:40,507
That the Reading Steiner is yours alone...

518
00:31:41,877 --> 00:31:43,267
Do you dislike that?

519
00:31:43,267 --> 00:31:45,217
Not really, but...

520
00:31:45,567 --> 00:31:49,177
For example, right now I'm here sewing your coat.

521
00:31:49,177 --> 00:31:54,397
It shouldn't be possible, but I have the impression that it's happened before.

522
00:31:55,267 --> 00:31:57,367
You want to say it's déjà vu, don't you?

523
00:31:57,367 --> 00:32:02,157
I did too. But it happens so often when I'm with you.

524
00:32:03,487 --> 00:32:08,367
Tell me, have I done this same thing in another world line?

525
00:32:10,367 --> 00:32:12,047
I knew I did.

526
00:32:13,417 --> 00:32:14,327
What's your point?

527
00:32:14,937 --> 00:32:17,707
Déjà vu is considered to be

528
00:32:17,707 --> 00:32:22,677
an anomaly caused by the overlapping of short-term memory and long-term memory.

529
00:32:22,677 --> 00:32:26,387
In other words, it's a phenomenon created by a temporal discrepancy of memories.

530
00:32:26,387 --> 00:32:28,847
Reading Steiner is the retention

531
00:32:28,847 --> 00:32:34,137
of memories of multiple world lines generated by the alteration of the past.

532
00:32:34,137 --> 00:32:40,027
Thus, both are memory anomalies created in the brain by temporal misplacement.

533
00:32:40,347 --> 00:32:44,277
I actually just confirmed a different world line occurrence

534
00:32:44,967 --> 00:32:47,737
based on a memory I had acknowledged as déjà vu.

535
00:32:48,827 --> 00:32:53,257
You're saying that déjà vu is a form of Reading Steiner?

536
00:32:53,257 --> 00:32:56,957
It may be difficult to demonstrate, but it's possible.

537
00:32:57,647 --> 00:33:00,587
I plan to write a paper on it after I get back.

538
00:33:02,027 --> 00:33:05,047
No matter where you go, you never change.

539
00:33:05,397 --> 00:33:07,297
You experiment-loving girl!

540
00:33:07,297 --> 00:33:09,467
I'll take that as a compliment.

541
00:33:09,467 --> 00:33:13,847
Anyway, if anything happens, let me know.

542
00:33:14,157 --> 00:33:15,057
That's—

543
00:33:29,097 --> 00:33:30,647
Tutturu~

544
00:33:30,647 --> 00:33:32,367
It's lunch time!

545
00:33:32,957 --> 00:33:36,657
Mayushii, did you bring my lunch?

546
00:33:36,657 --> 00:33:37,517
Yep.

547
00:33:37,517 --> 00:33:42,717
Today's lunch is the new Juicy
 Karaage Number 1 boxed lunch!

548
00:33:42,717 --> 00:33:45,497
Didn't we have that yesterday?

549
00:33:45,497 --> 00:33:46,807
Another invention?

550
00:33:46,807 --> 00:33:47,547
Yup.

551
00:33:47,547 --> 00:33:52,847
I was upgrading the Future Gadget No. 10 Cool Visitor.

552
00:33:52,847 --> 00:33:54,387
Now it's perfect!

553
00:33:54,387 --> 00:33:57,517
You love inventing stuff, don't you, Daru?

554
00:33:57,517 --> 00:34:03,057
That's why I started the Future Gadget Lab, duh.

555
00:34:04,667 --> 00:34:06,647
It's Kurisu!

556
00:34:07,207 --> 00:34:09,007
What's wrong?

557
00:34:09,807 --> 00:34:11,157
Where is he?

558
00:34:12,027 --> 00:34:13,347
He?

559
00:34:13,347 --> 00:34:14,897
That guy!

560
00:34:14,897 --> 00:34:18,347
We were at the laundromat and all of a sudden, he was gone.

561
00:34:20,427 --> 00:34:21,837
Like I said, who?

562
00:34:21,837 --> 00:34:25,987
You know, that guy who's always here...

563
00:34:25,987 --> 00:34:27,587
The founder of this lab.

564
00:34:28,417 --> 00:34:29,747
Of this lab?

565
00:34:29,747 --> 00:34:31,007
That would be me.

566
00:34:31,007 --> 00:34:33,137
What?! What are you saying?

567
00:34:33,137 --> 00:34:35,807
Oh, do you mean Ruka?

568
00:34:35,807 --> 00:34:37,057
No!

569
00:34:37,057 --> 00:34:40,207
Faris? Or Miss Kiryuu?

570
00:34:40,207 --> 00:34:43,457
Not them! You know, that...

571
00:34:43,457 --> 00:34:45,647
Right! Lab Member No. 001...

572
00:34:45,647 --> 00:34:47,247
001?

573
00:34:47,247 --> 00:34:49,067
001 is a vacant number.

574
00:34:49,567 --> 00:34:52,327
We told you before, Kurisu.

575
00:34:52,327 --> 00:34:55,537
We're keeping 001 open.

576
00:34:55,537 --> 00:34:57,367
But...

577
00:34:58,247 --> 00:35:00,357
Then what about this lab coat?

578
00:35:00,357 --> 00:35:03,377
That's yours, Kurisu.

579
00:35:03,377 --> 00:35:04,507
Mine?

580
00:35:09,327 --> 00:35:10,377
You're right.

581
00:35:11,257 --> 00:35:14,127
Why was I in a panic?

582
00:35:15,157 --> 00:35:19,217
Mayushii was wondering what happened.

583
00:35:19,217 --> 00:35:20,007
Sorry.

584
00:35:20,007 --> 00:35:21,917
Have you gone nuts, Miss Makise?

585
00:35:21,917 --> 00:35:22,857
I haven't!

586
00:35:24,297 --> 00:35:29,917
<i>I think that was the first moment I felt something was out of place.</i>

587
00:35:33,567 --> 00:35:34,907
<i>Something was missing.</i>

588
00:35:35,757 --> 00:35:41,797
<i>Something I thought existed wasn't there anymore.</i>

589
00:35:41,797 --> 00:35:43,997
<i>It's definitely something, but...</i>

590
00:35:45,467 --> 00:35:47,807
<i>I don't know what it is.</i>

591
00:35:49,407 --> 00:35:54,427
<i>Something felt off, as if this world wasn't real. Like it was fake.</i>

592
00:35:55,057 --> 00:35:58,887
<i>There was an uneasy feeling that something was manipulating my memory.</i>

593
00:35:59,987 --> 00:36:04,647
<i>At the same time, I wondered if it was all just a delusion</i>

594
00:36:05,057 --> 00:36:09,567
<i>and feared I was going crazy...</i>

595
00:36:13,807 --> 00:36:18,497
<i>A restless urge to recall and the temptation</i>

596
00:36:18,497 --> 00:36:22,867
<i>to forget everything to achieve peace of mind were clashing constantly.</i>

597
00:36:26,567 --> 00:36:31,127
<i>A week later, just as that uncomfortable feeling was fading...</i>

