Stupid.

1861
00:56:50,477 --> 00:56:53,667
<i>Stupid! Why...</i>

1862
00:56:53,667 --> 00:56:55,307
<i>Why?!</i>

1863
00:56:55,897 --> 00:56:58,657
<i>Now it's like I'm the stupid one!</i>

1864
00:56:58,657 --> 00:57:02,127
<i>Being told some obscure nonsense, getting pushed around...</i>

1865
00:57:02,127 --> 00:57:03,697
<i>Getting told "I love you"</i>

1866
00:57:04,097 --> 00:57:06,027
<i>and not being able to forget you...</i>

1867
00:57:06,697 --> 00:57:09,367
<i>At this rate, if this...</i>

1868
00:57:10,747 --> 00:57:12,097
Okarin!

1869
00:57:13,037 --> 00:57:15,417
This is Dr Pepper color, isn't it?

1870
00:57:15,757 --> 00:57:19,667
Yes, the very embodiment of intelligence.

1871
00:57:21,647 --> 00:57:24,387
Requesting to see you in it, Mayushii.

1872
00:57:24,387 --> 00:57:25,887
Silence, Perverted Gentleman.

1873
00:57:30,067 --> 00:57:32,347
<i>Okabe! Okabe!</i>

1874
00:57:37,727 --> 00:57:38,647
What was that?!

1875
00:57:39,687 --> 00:57:41,727
<i>There's no way I can forget you...</i>

1876
00:57:42,737 --> 00:57:46,817
<i>Because I've known you for a long, long time...</i>

1877
00:57:47,787 --> 00:57:51,037
<i>And I've loved you for a long, long time...</i>

1878
00:57:54,077 --> 00:57:56,787
<i>And I will always...</i>

1879
00:57:57,867 --> 00:57:59,077
<i>Always...</i>

1880
00:58:03,507 --> 00:58:05,127
Okarin?

1881
00:58:06,867 --> 00:58:09,797
It's nothing... I'm fine.

1882
00:58:12,597 --> 00:58:14,057
Kurisu!

1883
00:58:16,887 --> 00:58:18,397
Okabe!

1884
00:58:19,107 --> 00:58:20,057
Kurisu...

1885
00:58:20,567 --> 00:58:22,727
Okabe, I—

1886
00:58:34,027 --> 00:58:36,927
Mayushii! Tissue! Tissue! Quick!

1887
00:58:36,927 --> 00:58:40,037
Y-Yes! Tissue! Tissue!

1888
00:58:40,037 --> 00:58:41,247
There! There!

1889
00:58:47,997 --> 00:58:49,637
Kurisu?

1890
00:58:49,637 --> 00:58:50,717
What's up?

1891
00:58:54,027 --> 00:58:55,457
Where is he?

1892
00:58:55,457 --> 00:58:56,687
He?

1893
00:58:56,687 --> 00:59:00,397
That guy... He was just there...

1894
00:59:00,397 --> 00:59:01,717
Like I said. Who?

1895
00:59:01,717 --> 00:59:05,597
You know... That guy!

1896
00:59:05,597 --> 00:59:08,737
The one who's always here, the founder of this lab...

1897
00:59:09,397 --> 00:59:10,797
Of this lab?

1898
00:59:13,527 --> 00:59:15,197
That's me.

1899
00:59:27,907 --> 00:59:32,347
Okabe... Rintarou

1900
00:59:34,167 --> 00:59:39,187
Yes... Okabe... Rintarou...

1901
00:59:46,317 --> 00:59:49,057
What's wrong, Kurisu?

1902
00:59:49,057 --> 00:59:50,487
Did you run into a pervert?

1903
01:00:08,837 --> 01:00:11,177
Hashida! Lend me your cell phone!

1904
01:00:11,177 --> 01:00:12,757
What? Why?

1905
01:00:12,757 --> 01:00:16,477
Just do it! Then hack into SERN immediately.

1906
01:00:16,477 --> 01:00:17,187
Wha—?!

1907
01:00:17,187 --> 01:00:17,967
Hurry!

1908
01:00:18,477 --> 01:00:23,327
<i>It's wrong! I won't accept it!</i>

1909
01:00:23,327 --> 01:00:25,467
<i>No matter what you tell me...</i>

1910
01:00:27,547 --> 01:00:30,317
That's no good, Kurisu.

1911
01:00:31,317 --> 01:00:32,487
Mayuri...

1912
01:00:32,487 --> 01:00:35,757
Mayushii doesn't really understand, but...

1913
01:00:35,757 --> 01:00:38,737
Mayushii thinks it'll only hurt you.

1914
01:00:49,847 --> 01:00:52,987
<i>That's when I made my decision</i>

1915
01:00:55,827 --> 01:00:59,027
<i>to accept your wish.</i>

1916
01:01:00,807 --> 01:01:04,707
<i>I won't manipulate time or the past</i>

1917
01:01:05,267 --> 01:01:08,767
<i>and will accept this world you fiercely protected</i>

1918
01:01:07,057 --> 01:01:08,767
Future Gadget Lab

1919
01:01:08,767 --> 01:01:10,817
<i>as reality.</i>

1920
01:01:11,147 --> 01:01:13,777
<i>I will forget my memories of you</i>

1921
01:01:13,777 --> 01:01:16,407
<i>and the name Okabe Rintarou,</i>

1922
01:01:17,917 --> 01:01:23,187
<i>and I'll just keep walking towards the unknown future...</i>

1923
01:01:24,107 --> 01:01:27,997
<i>because that's what you wanted.</i>

1924
01:01:33,207 --> 01:01:34,957
Oh, Daru?

1925
01:01:35,627 --> 01:01:37,467
You're not coming today, either?

1926
01:01:37,467 --> 01:01:41,807
It's too hot at the lab! And there's the Rai-Net tournament today.

1927
01:01:42,097 --> 01:01:42,857
Oh...

1928
01:01:42,857 --> 01:01:47,257
<i>Why don't you come too, Mayushii? Do a twin battle with Faris!</i>

1929
01:01:47,257 --> 01:01:50,277
But I'm not on shift today...

1930
01:01:50,277 --> 01:01:51,687
<i>See you later, then.</i>

1931
01:01:51,687 --> 01:01:52,577
<i>Yeah.</i>

1932
01:01:59,497 --> 01:02:01,317
<i>Are you ready?</i>

1933
01:02:01,317 --> 01:02:04,037
<i>We will now initiate Operation Midgard!</i>

1934
01:02:17,467 --> 01:02:20,257
Moeka! What's wrong?

1935
01:02:21,217 --> 01:02:22,687
He wants to talk to you...

1936
01:02:23,437 --> 01:02:24,687
The Manager...

1937
01:02:25,527 --> 01:02:30,097
In other words, there is also the theory that we still haven't reached

1938
01:02:30,097 --> 01:02:32,647
a correct neuroscientific conclusion on why

1939
01:02:32,647 --> 01:02:36,067
the phenomenon known as "dreaming" occurs, nor what it is needed for.

1940
01:02:36,517 --> 01:02:41,487
I will continue on this subject in our next lecture.

1941
01:02:41,487 --> 01:02:42,867
Brain

1942
01:02:41,487 --> 01:02:42,987
Confusion

1943
01:02:41,487 --> 01:02:42,867
Mystery

1944
01:02:42,867 --> 01:02:42,987
Brain

1945
01:02:42,867 --> 01:02:42,987
Mystery

1946
01:02:42,987 --> 01:02:43,737
Brain

1947
01:02:42,987 --> 01:02:43,117
Confusion

1948
01:02:42,987 --> 01:02:43,117
Mystery

1949
01:02:43,117 --> 01:02:43,237
Confusion

1950
01:02:43,117 --> 01:02:43,237
Mystery

1951
01:02:43,237 --> 01:02:43,487
Confusion

1952
01:02:43,237 --> 01:02:43,487
Mystery

1953
01:02:43,487 --> 01:02:43,617
Confusion

1954
01:02:43,487 --> 01:02:43,617
Mystery

1955
01:02:43,617 --> 01:02:43,737
Mystery

1956
01:02:43,737 --> 01:02:44,247
Mystery

1957
01:02:44,247 --> 01:02:44,367
Mystery

1958
01:02:58,187 --> 01:03:02,447
I need to decide where to go for dinner.

1959
01:03:04,747 --> 01:03:07,347
Well, we can't do anything about it.

1960
01:03:07,347 --> 01:03:08,657
Are you serious?

1961
01:03:09,357 --> 01:03:13,267
Mayushii tried to save her pocket money too, but it's not enough...

1962
01:03:13,797 --> 01:03:16,647
So you're giving up? We'll lose the lab.

1963
01:03:17,137 --> 01:03:19,487
Why are you so upset, Miss Makise?

1964
01:03:21,297 --> 01:03:22,487
I...

1965
01:03:22,487 --> 01:03:28,977
Lately, I've just started to feel like it's a pain to pay the rent.

1966
01:03:28,977 --> 01:03:30,657
Mayushii didn't realize...

1967
01:03:30,657 --> 01:03:34,227
I started this lab because I thought that maybe we could do something,

1968
01:03:34,227 --> 01:03:35,877
but in the end...

1969
01:03:35,877 --> 01:03:40,007
What's going to happen to Mayuri?! She won't have a place to go!

1970
01:03:40,007 --> 01:03:43,387
Mayushii will be okay. Mayushii has the café.

1971
01:03:43,847 --> 01:03:44,907
Mayuri...

1972
01:03:45,697 --> 01:03:48,807
Actually, Mayushii was feeling the same way.

1973
01:03:49,237 --> 01:03:54,777
Lately, when Mayushii comes to the lab, Mayushii gets kind of lonely...

1974
01:03:55,627 --> 01:03:57,817
It's like...

1975
01:03:58,287 --> 01:04:00,537
Something's missing...

1976
01:04:02,297 --> 01:04:05,447
What is?

1977
01:04:06,867 --> 01:04:10,577
The thing is... Mayushii doesn't know what.

1978
01:04:12,527 --> 01:04:13,827
I see...

1979
01:04:14,817 --> 01:04:15,897
See you, then.

1980
01:04:15,897 --> 01:04:21,587
The lab won't close right away. I'll email you, okay?

1981
01:04:21,587 --> 01:04:22,767
Okay...

1982
01:04:22,767 --> 01:04:25,237
Cheer up, Kurisu.

1983
01:04:25,237 --> 01:04:27,057
Thank you. I'll be fine.

1984
01:04:28,327 --> 01:04:30,157
I'm going, then.

1985
01:04:35,267 --> 01:04:37,727
Address does not exist.
    The lab might be dissolved.
     To: Okabe Rintarou

1986
01:04:35,267 --> 01:04:37,727
Address does not exist.
    The lab might be dissolved.
     To: Okabe Rintarou

1987
01:04:41,357 --> 01:04:44,897
This is reality. This is the world...

1988
01:04:44,897 --> 01:04:48,407
Exactly. This world line's reality.

1989
01:04:50,797 --> 01:04:54,127
I thought I'd at least come to say hello.

1990
01:04:54,747 --> 01:04:57,037
I decided to go back to the future.

1991
01:04:59,097 --> 01:05:01,957
If you've decided to accept a world

1992
01:05:01,957 --> 01:05:06,127
where Okabe Rintarou doesn't exist, there's no point in me remaining.

1993
01:05:07,977 --> 01:05:10,657
I'll ask you one last time.

1994
01:05:10,657 --> 01:05:12,097
Aren't you going to change your mind?

1995
01:05:13,407 --> 01:05:19,397
There's no record of Okabe Rintarou on this world line from this point now on.

1996
01:05:19,977 --> 01:05:24,697
In other words, once I go back, you'll never see him again.

1997
01:05:24,997 --> 01:05:26,697
Is that still what you want?

1998
01:05:28,907 --> 01:05:34,207
Okabe told me not to change the past, no matter what happens.

1999
01:05:34,887 --> 01:05:38,247
I agree with him. The risks are too—

2000
01:05:38,247 --> 01:05:41,757
That's not my question! What does your heart tell you!?

2001
01:05:42,917 --> 01:05:46,507
I won't... change... my mind.

2002
01:05:47,777 --> 01:05:49,967
So that's how it's going to be...

2003
01:05:51,367 --> 01:05:55,347
You know, in the future, you'll build the time machine.

2004
01:05:56,247 --> 01:05:57,307
What do you mean?

2005
01:05:57,307 --> 01:06:00,497
Makise Kurisu develops the time machine.

2006
01:06:00,497 --> 01:06:04,817
But she won't authorize its use, and will ask my father to seal it off,

2007
01:06:04,817 --> 01:06:07,487
saying that it's the will of Okabe Rintarou.

2008
01:06:07,997 --> 01:06:11,467
In other words, you'll keep contradicting yourself.

2009
01:06:11,467 --> 01:06:16,167
You'll find a way to return to the past to help and see him,

2010
01:06:16,167 --> 01:06:18,207
and even build the time machine,

2011
01:06:18,207 --> 01:06:22,457
but you'll give up in the end because you can't be honest with yourself.

2012
01:06:22,457 --> 01:06:24,667
You'll do this over and over again.

2013
01:06:25,357 --> 01:06:27,007
That's why you—

2014
01:06:27,267 --> 01:06:32,707
I thought that the you of the past might be more true to yourself.

2015
01:06:35,157 --> 01:06:37,687
But you're still the same stubborn girl.

2016
01:06:38,457 --> 01:06:40,227
How can you—

2017
01:06:40,567 --> 01:06:41,477
It's the truth.

2018
01:06:41,477 --> 01:06:43,727
I am a scientist!

2019
01:06:43,727 --> 01:06:46,027
My actions are based on my theories and my beliefs.

2020
01:06:46,357 --> 01:06:48,737
I can't be swayed by emotion—

2021
01:06:48,737 --> 01:06:51,597
You always pretend to be cool-headed like that!

2022
01:06:51,597 --> 01:06:54,197
You really get on my nerves!

2023
01:06:54,497 --> 01:06:55,957
It's the same for me!

2024
01:06:57,227 --> 01:06:59,707
Okabe Rintarou is no more...

2025
01:07:00,397 --> 01:07:02,337
but the world keeps on going.

2026
01:07:02,757 --> 01:07:05,837
It keeps on going as if nothing ever happened.

2027
01:07:06,707 --> 01:07:09,007
But you'll build the time machine.

2028
01:07:09,967 --> 01:07:11,757
What's more important to you?

2029
01:07:11,757 --> 01:07:14,217
Your pride and ethical code as a scientist?

2030
01:07:14,547 --> 01:07:16,187
Is that enough for you?

2031
01:07:16,187 --> 01:07:19,277
Is there a reason for you to live in this world?

2032
01:07:27,497 --> 01:07:29,607
This is the time machine?

2033
01:07:29,607 --> 01:07:30,357
Let's go.

2034
01:07:30,997 --> 01:07:32,837
Is it really possible?

2035
01:07:32,837 --> 01:07:35,427
The future you said it was.

2036
01:07:35,427 --> 01:07:38,817
If you change the past, the world line will shift.

2037
01:07:38,817 --> 01:07:41,547
That's why you won't change any of the events that occurred,

2038
01:07:41,547 --> 01:07:43,917
but only alter Okabe Rintarou's memory.

2039
01:07:44,257 --> 01:07:45,377
His memory...

2040
01:07:45,377 --> 01:07:48,727
Okabe Rintarou is unable to recognize the Steins Gate

2041
01:07:48,727 --> 01:07:51,677
world line as the real world.

2042
01:07:51,677 --> 01:07:55,347
So you only need to make him recognize that this world line

2043
01:07:55,347 --> 01:07:58,267
is distinctly different from the others.

2044
01:07:58,267 --> 01:08:00,647
That's why I have to alter his memory?

2045
01:08:02,327 --> 01:08:03,747
Yes.

2046
01:08:03,747 --> 01:08:07,827
Anchor a powerful memory that isn't present in any other world line.

2047
01:08:07,827 --> 01:08:12,507
Then the present world line will be imprinted on his brain as something distinctly different

2048
01:08:12,507 --> 01:08:17,537
from the others, and he will be freed from his Reading Steiner overload.

2049
01:08:18,037 --> 01:08:21,537
That does sound correct in theory. True to my reputation.

2050
01:08:21,537 --> 01:08:25,157
But you didn't even try to go to the past.

2051
01:08:25,157 --> 01:08:26,167
Sit down over there.

2052
01:08:26,487 --> 01:08:30,047
That was my scientist's conscience. You should be praising me.

2053
01:08:30,367 --> 01:08:31,507
Narcissist...

2054
01:08:31,507 --> 01:08:36,967
How rude! It's not like that, I'm just... a scientist.

2055
01:08:36,967 --> 01:08:41,947
You're just like her. Well, you're the same person after all.

2056
01:08:42,457 --> 01:08:45,277
Come on, let's go. To what year?

2057
01:08:45,277 --> 01:08:46,367
You don't know?

2058
01:08:46,367 --> 01:08:48,937
You should know better than me

2059
01:08:48,937 --> 01:08:53,317
when the best time to plant a powerful memory in Okabe Rintarou's brain would be.

2060
01:08:55,997 --> 01:08:57,327
2005.

2061
01:08:57,327 --> 01:08:58,437
Based on what?

2062
01:08:58,437 --> 01:09:01,087
Something Mayuri told me.

2063
01:09:01,087 --> 01:09:04,827
Powerful memories are generated by powerful events.

2064
01:09:05,447 --> 01:09:07,777
Gotcha. I'll trust you.

2065
01:09:08,377 --> 01:09:11,597
Let's go! The force is a bit strong, so be prepared!

2066
01:09:28,687 --> 01:09:32,147
Now it's up to you. You have no cell phone, so to get in touch—

2067
01:09:32,147 --> 01:09:35,297
Wait! What am I supposed to do?

2068
01:09:35,297 --> 01:09:38,867
I already told you the objective, but I don't know

2069
01:09:39,157 --> 01:09:43,447
how to plant a powerful memory in Okabe Rintarou's head.

2070
01:09:43,447 --> 01:09:46,037
You said you would know what to do.

2071
01:09:46,037 --> 01:09:47,767
The future me did?

2072
01:09:47,767 --> 01:09:48,647
Yes.

2073
01:09:51,007 --> 01:09:53,617
<i>I found Mayuri's address, but there was no way</i>

2074
01:09:53,617 --> 01:09:57,797
<i>to obtain Okabe's after he had disappeared from this world line.</i>

2075
01:09:55,047 --> 01:09:57,797
Shiina

2076
01:09:58,667 --> 01:10:02,547
<i>It should be near this house, but...</i>

2077
01:10:02,547 --> 01:10:04,487
<i>If I find him, then what?</i>

2078
01:10:04,487 --> 01:10:06,937
<i>How do I talk to him? What do I do?</i>

2079
01:10:07,207 --> 01:10:09,197
<i>If I fail...</i>

2080
01:10:09,197 --> 01:10:13,697
<i>A change in the past will always affect something else.</i>

2081
01:10:13,697 --> 01:10:17,317
<i>It will never change in a way that's convenient for you.</i>

2082
01:10:29,887 --> 01:10:31,397
Okabe?

2083
01:10:39,637 --> 01:10:41,217
Okabe!

2084
01:10:43,767 --> 01:10:45,637
Okabe! Okabe!

2085
01:10:46,977 --> 01:10:49,557
Wait! I need to talk to you!

2086
01:11:05,407 --> 01:11:09,107
Don't worry. The world will return to normal.

2087
01:11:09,107 --> 01:11:14,297
Right... Okabe is never ever going to die there!

2088
01:11:14,727 --> 01:11:18,067
It's all right. There's no need to worry about it!

2089
01:11:18,447 --> 01:11:22,887
But I keep wondering... If I return to the past again,

2090
01:11:23,297 --> 01:11:26,827
will Okabe get hit by a car again?

2091
01:11:26,827 --> 01:11:30,347
Or perhaps an even more terrifying change will occur.

2092
01:11:31,047 --> 01:11:35,407
If I interfere, something like that could easily happen...

2093
01:11:35,407 --> 01:11:39,297
But the Okabe Rintarou of that time won't die anyway.

2094
01:11:39,297 --> 01:11:41,377
Don't you understand, Amane?

2095
01:11:41,377 --> 01:11:43,237
The fact that Okabe absolutely won't die

2096
01:11:43,797 --> 01:11:47,927
also means that I absolutely won't be able to help him!

2097
01:11:47,927 --> 01:11:49,767
But the future you—

2098
01:11:49,767 --> 01:11:53,497
Okabe had to endure this feeling of powerlessness

2099
01:11:54,307 --> 01:11:56,457
all by himself, all this time!

2100
01:11:57,637 --> 01:11:59,467
I couldn't possibly...

2101
01:12:04,887 --> 01:12:06,967
<i>Let's see, this is...</i>

2102
01:12:12,447 --> 01:12:14,377
Oh, Kurisu!

2103
01:12:14,377 --> 01:12:15,877
Tutturu~

2104
01:12:15,877 --> 01:12:16,847
Hello.

2105
01:12:16,847 --> 01:12:20,707
Say, is this "furniture" or "audio"?

2106
01:12:20,707 --> 01:12:22,327
Are you throwing that away?

2107
01:12:22,327 --> 01:12:24,247
Yeah. Daru told me

2108
01:12:24,247 --> 01:12:26,827
to just stick the disposal ticket on it.

2109
01:12:27,357 --> 01:12:28,377
I see.

2110
01:12:30,107 --> 01:12:32,217
It's kind of sad, isn't it?

2111
01:12:33,257 --> 01:12:34,457
Yes.

2112
01:12:34,727 --> 01:12:36,917
But that's how it is.

2113
01:12:39,767 --> 01:12:41,877
Listen, Kurisu.

2114
01:12:45,317 --> 01:12:48,807
Do you know about... "Okarin"?

2115
01:12:50,267 --> 01:12:56,397
You see, when I'm here, sometimes that word just pops into my head

2116
01:12:56,397 --> 01:13:00,087
while I'm tidying up or making costumes,

2117
01:13:00,087 --> 01:13:02,107
or even eating...

2118
01:13:09,687 --> 01:13:11,327
I don't...

2119
01:13:12,627 --> 01:13:14,077
Kurisu?

2120
01:13:21,127 --> 01:13:22,797
Makise!

2121
01:13:22,797 --> 01:13:24,637
Urushibara...

2122
01:13:26,907 --> 01:13:28,057
You're training hard.

2123
01:13:28,057 --> 01:13:34,057
Yes. I do 100 swings a day to
 unleash Samidare's true power.

2124
01:13:34,057 --> 01:13:37,517
Interesting name. Did you choose it?

2125
01:13:37,517 --> 01:13:38,647
Yes...

2126
01:13:39,557 --> 01:13:41,107
No, it wasn't—

2127
01:13:42,987 --> 01:13:45,567
This katana...

2128
01:13:46,277 --> 01:13:48,697
I think someone gave it to me.

2129
01:13:52,897 --> 01:13:54,577
<i>Stop it!</i>

2130
01:13:59,537 --> 01:14:01,027
It's a virus, nyan~!

2131
01:14:01,757 --> 01:14:05,257
It feels so good to get beaten up by you, Faris!

2132
01:14:05,667 --> 01:14:06,717
8-0

2133
01:14:06,717 --> 01:14:08,797
It's so one-sided.

2134
01:14:10,927 --> 01:14:13,777
Kurisu showed up!

2135
01:14:13,777 --> 01:14:14,977
What are you doing?

2136
01:14:14,977 --> 01:14:17,727
We were doing a Rai-Net battle at MayQueen when

2137
01:14:17,727 --> 01:14:22,067
Faris suddenly said she wanted to play against the head of the lab!

2138
01:14:22,067 --> 01:14:26,277
She summoned me on my way back from a part-time job interview!

2139
01:14:26,277 --> 01:14:26,907
An interview?

2140
01:14:26,907 --> 01:14:27,617
Yup.

2141
01:14:27,617 --> 01:14:30,747
I want to try to at least be able to pay the lab's rent.

2142
01:14:30,747 --> 01:14:32,907
It's better if the lab exists, don't you think?

2143
01:14:33,307 --> 01:14:34,427
Hashida...

2144
01:14:35,497 --> 01:14:37,957
But something's different, nyan~.

2145
01:14:37,957 --> 01:14:40,227
The head of the lab used to play...

2146
01:14:40,227 --> 01:14:41,037
Better?

2147
01:14:41,347 --> 01:14:45,457
No. He sucked, nyan~. Catastrophically.

2148
01:14:45,457 --> 01:14:49,177
But I think he was much livelier, nyan~!

2149
01:14:51,987 --> 01:14:53,327
Like a real battle?

2150
01:14:53,327 --> 01:14:56,087
No, nyan~! But like...

2151
01:14:56,087 --> 01:14:58,867
Daru-nyan, strike a pose, nyan~!

2152
01:14:58,867 --> 01:15:00,687
Like this?

2153
01:15:01,117 --> 01:15:03,647
No, nyan~!

2154
01:15:04,477 --> 01:15:06,147
I think I understand...

2155
01:15:06,587 --> 01:15:08,277
There should be one more...

2156
01:15:08,567 --> 01:15:10,477
One more?

2157
01:15:10,477 --> 01:15:12,447
But he's not here...

2158
01:15:13,337 --> 01:15:14,287
Déjà vu!

2159
01:15:15,517 --> 01:15:20,417
As I suspected, it's not a delusion your brain is showing you.

2160
01:15:20,417 --> 01:15:23,207
Déjà vu is a manifestation of Reading Steiner!

2161
01:15:23,827 --> 01:15:25,547
They're memories of another world line...

2162
01:15:25,847 --> 01:15:28,417
I exist on countless world lines.

2163
01:15:28,417 --> 01:15:31,857
The convergence of those lines and all those memories coming together

2164
01:15:31,857 --> 01:15:33,057
makes me who I am now.

2165
01:15:33,587 --> 01:15:35,677
A one and only me.

2166
01:15:36,027 --> 01:15:39,437
<i>Your mightily annoying self won't disappear from anyone's heart.</i>

2167
01:15:39,827 --> 01:15:43,387
<i>Even when you think you've been forgotten, our memories of you</i>

2168
01:15:43,387 --> 01:15:44,477
<i>will always remain somewhere...</i>

2169
01:15:46,907 --> 01:15:48,867
<i>I tried to give up.</i>

2170
01:15:49,327 --> 01:15:51,807
<i>I tried to forget so many times.</i>

2171
01:15:52,347 --> 01:15:55,307
<i>I thought it'd be impossible, even with the time machine.</i>

2172
01:15:55,307 --> 01:15:59,467
<i>But I feel like everyone is telling me not to forget!</i>

2173
01:16:00,267 --> 01:16:01,627
<i>I...</i>

2174
01:16:01,627 --> 01:16:04,207
Ku-nyan? What's wrong, nyan~?

2175
01:16:05,397 --> 01:16:06,697
I am...

2176
01:16:08,627 --> 01:16:10,877
Hououin Kyouma!

2177
01:16:10,877 --> 01:16:14,457
My goal is to reform this world's ruling structure!

2178
01:16:14,457 --> 01:16:17,847
To accomplish this, the Future Gadget Lab

2179
01:16:17,847 --> 01:16:22,147
must develop an invention that will plunge the world into chaos!

2180
01:16:25,207 --> 01:16:28,247
Did the heat make you go nuts?

2181
01:16:28,247 --> 01:16:30,257
But I've seen this before, nyan~.

2182
01:16:30,257 --> 01:16:30,947
<i>Stop it...</i>

2183
01:16:30,947 --> 01:16:32,727
Be silent, Supah Hakah!

2184
01:16:32,727 --> 01:16:34,947
I am a mad scientist!

2185
01:16:35,207 --> 01:16:38,277
That's the scenario again? Wait.

2186
01:16:38,277 --> 01:16:39,157
What am I saying?

2187
01:16:39,647 --> 01:16:40,987
<i>Don't remember!</i>

2188
01:16:41,617 --> 01:16:44,577
Mayuri! The intellectual beverage of the chosen ones!

2189
01:16:44,577 --> 01:16:46,417
Good evening... Oh?

2190
01:16:46,417 --> 01:16:48,757
Rukako! Don't neglect your practice swings!

2191
01:16:48,757 --> 01:16:49,757
Y-Yes, sir!

2192
01:16:49,757 --> 01:16:53,567
The hidden power of the demon sword Samidare can only be unlocked

2193
01:16:53,567 --> 01:16:55,387
through sheer discipline!

2194
01:16:55,387 --> 01:16:56,357
Yes, sir!

2195
01:16:57,097 --> 01:16:59,997
<i>It's useless... I can't help him...</i>

2196
01:17:01,227 --> 01:17:04,237
Here you go, Kurisu. Your Dr Pepper.

2197
01:17:06,967 --> 01:17:10,857
But you know, Kurisu, you aren't Hououin Kyouma.

2198
01:17:11,467 --> 01:17:13,507
Hououin Kyouma is...

2199
01:17:15,957 --> 01:17:17,617
Hououin Kyouma is...

2200
01:17:19,687 --> 01:17:21,077
Okabe Rintarou...

2201
01:17:22,637 --> 01:17:24,477
Okabe Rintarou...

2202
01:17:26,137 --> 01:17:27,997
Oka... rin?

2203
01:17:27,997 --> 01:17:33,007
Okarin? Sounds familiar. But my mind is still fuzzy.

2204
01:17:33,007 --> 01:17:35,757
Okarin? Do you mean Kyouma, nyan~?

2205
01:17:36,287 --> 01:17:38,007
...Okabe?

2206
01:17:38,357 --> 01:17:41,017
Oka... Kyouma!

2207
01:17:42,267 --> 01:17:45,767
Okarin... Okarin...

2208
01:17:47,677 --> 01:17:49,747
I don't know who that is,

2209
01:17:49,747 --> 01:17:55,487
but when I say his name, I feel warm inside.

2210
01:17:56,127 --> 01:17:58,277
I wonder why.

2211
01:18:07,977 --> 01:18:11,047
<i>Everyone is watching something other than themselves,</i>

2212
01:18:11,047 --> 01:18:13,127
<i>something important to them,</i>

2213
01:18:13,807 --> 01:18:16,637
<i>just like you did when you were observing us.</i>

2214
01:18:19,867 --> 01:18:22,767
<i>Even if you're not in this world...</i>

2215
01:18:23,107 --> 01:18:24,677
<i>Even if there's no trace of you here...</i>

2216
01:18:26,007 --> 01:18:28,727
<i>People's feelings will still cross world lines.</i>

2217
01:18:30,857 --> 01:18:31,997
<i>But...</i>

2218
01:18:35,697 --> 01:18:39,717
<i>Soon, Okabe will pass by, just like before.</i>

2219
01:18:41,197 --> 01:18:44,287
<i>I've made it this far, but I don't know what to do.</i>

2220
01:18:49,707 --> 01:18:51,837
<i>How can I save him?</i>

2221
01:18:52,537 --> 01:18:56,867
<i>Even if our feelings cross world lines, the events will still revert back!</i>

2222
01:18:56,867 --> 01:18:58,987
<i>Then what can I do?</i>

2223
01:18:59,417 --> 01:19:01,617
<i>Whatever I do will be useless!</i>

2224
01:19:02,227 --> 01:19:03,747
Don't you have an umbrella?

2225
01:19:08,187 --> 01:19:11,177
You're still wet! No umbrella?

2226
01:19:16,617 --> 01:19:20,657
<i>I don't know anything about Okabe.</i>

2227
01:19:21,187 --> 01:19:23,727
<i>All I have are fragments.</i>

2228
01:19:23,727 --> 01:19:26,547
<i>Slight memories from this world line</i>

2229
01:19:26,547 --> 01:19:29,937
<i>and the ones from other world lines, called déjà vu.</i>

2230
01:19:32,247 --> 01:19:38,227
<i>The past me would have never considered changing the past or building a time machine</i>

2231
01:19:38,227 --> 01:19:41,247
<i>because there was nothing I wanted to protect that badly.</i>

2232
01:19:43,097 --> 01:19:45,557
<i>But I finally found something...</i>

2233
01:19:46,517 --> 01:19:50,017
<i>I still haven't told him anything about how I feel...</i>

2234
01:19:53,537 --> 01:19:55,857
<i>Every time I saw him, I always acted stubborn</i>

2235
01:19:55,857 --> 01:19:57,777
<i>and quarreled with him.</i>

2236
01:19:57,777 --> 01:20:01,237
<i>I couldn't tell him what I really wanted to say.</i>

2237
01:20:08,587 --> 01:20:13,357
<i>Since I was little, I've always tried to do everything on my own</i>

2238
01:20:14,007 --> 01:20:16,087
<i>by building walls around me</i>

2239
01:20:16,367 --> 01:20:18,227
<i>and refusing any help.</i>

2240
01:20:18,727 --> 01:20:20,087
<i>An unpleasant child...</i>

2241
01:20:20,547 --> 01:20:23,117
<i>No wonder my father didn't like me.</i>

2242
01:20:24,537 --> 01:20:29,727
<i>But the truth is, I wanted someone to call out to me.</i>

2243
01:20:30,497 --> 01:20:32,767
<i>I wanted someone to say,</i>

2244
01:20:32,767 --> 01:20:36,857
<i>even if I was the only one there, "I'm here watching."</i>

2245
01:20:59,047 --> 01:21:00,357
Are you lost?

2246
01:21:06,327 --> 01:21:07,347
Me too.

2247
01:21:08,457 --> 01:21:13,867
A girl I've known since I was little is really depressed...

2248
01:21:15,467 --> 01:21:18,237
I don't know what to say to her...

2249
01:21:19,037 --> 01:21:22,867
I wonder if I'm just useless...

2250
01:21:34,617 --> 01:21:39,627
Have you heard of... Hououin Kyouma?

2251
01:21:40,867 --> 01:21:42,057
Hououin?

2252
01:21:42,587 --> 01:21:47,537
He's a scientist. But not just any scientist.

2253
01:21:47,537 --> 01:21:51,017
He's a mad scientist and a first-rate one at that.

2254
01:21:51,377 --> 01:21:54,017
He talked and behaved crazily,

2255
01:21:54,017 --> 01:21:56,397
and everyone always made a fool of him.

2256
01:21:57,197 --> 01:22:02,627
Nobody believed what he said, in his research, or in his discoveries.

2257
01:22:02,627 --> 01:22:07,157
But you know, what he uncovered was something that only he

2258
01:22:07,157 --> 01:22:08,907
could see.

2259
01:22:09,407 --> 01:22:13,087
He realized that it could hurt and cause pain

2260
01:22:13,087 --> 01:22:16,217
and even destroy the world at times.

2261
01:22:16,217 --> 01:22:20,207
So he tried with all his might to protect everyone.

2262
01:22:20,207 --> 01:22:23,437
He continued to fight to save the world

2263
01:22:25,227 --> 01:22:29,887
and managed to protect all of the people dear to him.

2264
01:22:30,877 --> 01:22:34,927
But nobody ever knew about it.

2265
01:22:35,307 --> 01:22:38,857
He went on being a mad scientist the entire time,

2266
01:22:39,457 --> 01:22:42,927
and everybody kept on making a fool of him.

2267
01:22:48,237 --> 01:22:50,987
That's a sad story.

2268
01:22:51,807 --> 01:22:55,877
Really? I think it's a wonderful story.

2269
01:23:01,297 --> 01:23:03,047
Go now.

2270
01:23:03,897 --> 01:23:06,407
I'm sure someone is waiting for you.

2271
01:23:20,727 --> 01:23:21,807
Mayuri!

2272
01:23:25,177 --> 01:23:26,687
Okarin?

2273
01:23:27,287 --> 01:23:29,697
I'm not letting them take you!

2274
01:23:30,017 --> 01:23:32,467
You're my hostage, Mayuri!

2275
01:23:32,467 --> 01:23:34,657
I'm going to use you for human experimentation!

2276
01:24:38,407 --> 01:24:43,487
<i>Are you ready? I will now give an overview of Operation Norn!</i>

2277
01:24:52,567 --> 01:24:54,737
What are you gawking at? Pervert!

2278
01:25:05,077 --> 01:25:06,127
You...

2279
01:25:07,837 --> 01:25:09,997
What are you doing here?

2280
01:25:14,557 --> 01:25:19,227
I didn't come to you. You're trying to come back

2281
01:25:19,887 --> 01:25:24,197
from this world to the Steins Gate world line.

2282
01:25:24,197 --> 01:25:28,067
Remember the times you wandered through the world lines?

2283
01:25:28,067 --> 01:25:30,527
I was always with you.

2284
01:25:30,527 --> 01:25:33,947
Mayuri, Hashida, Faris,

2285
01:25:34,247 --> 01:25:38,127
Urushibara, Kiryuu, and Amane

2286
01:25:38,127 --> 01:25:39,827
haven't forgotten you.

2287
01:25:41,377 --> 01:25:45,787
You were so arrogant to think that you were holding up the world by yourself!

2288
01:25:47,007 --> 01:25:48,267
Don't forget.

2289
01:25:48,877 --> 01:25:52,227
No matter what world line you're on, you'll never be alone.

2290
01:25:52,227 --> 01:25:55,127
I'll find you, wherever you are!

2291
01:25:55,127 --> 01:25:56,967
I will continue to observe you

2292
01:25:57,397 --> 01:26:00,757
just as you kept on observing me.

2293
01:26:16,457 --> 01:26:19,777
If that's the Steins Gate's choice.

2294
01:26:21,527 --> 01:26:25,207
Well, Cristina, care to return it to me?

2295
01:26:28,897 --> 01:26:31,167
...My first kiss.

2296
01:26:34,727 --> 01:26:35,747
Never.

2297
01:26:46,327 --> 01:26:52,557
Itsuka bokura ga mirai furikaeru toki ni wa

2298
01:26:46,327 --> 01:26:52,557
Someday in the future, we will look back

2299
01:26:50,057 --> 01:26:57,987
Load Region of Deja Vu

2300
01:26:50,057 --> 01:26:57,987
Load Region of Deja Vu

